   Hospitality (BIZMATOUR), Malacca, MALAYSIA, MAY 12-14, 2015},
Abstract = {The development of Islamic banks in Malaysia is increasingly challenging
   with more banks offering products and services based on Islamic
   principles. Full-fledged Islamic banks need to prepare and equip
   themselves to deal with the challenges ahead in order to be at the
   forefront of the Islamic banking industry. Undoubtedly, this requires a
   transformation in the financial and economic activities in accordance to
   those values and beliefs, which, among others, is to ensure that
   prohibition of giving and taking interest is upheld. One of the ways in
   which they could achieve this is through a reputable and diversified
   range of products and services, specifically, a desirable image that
   would boost confidence and enhance customers retention of their service
   provider. Hence, this study explores Shariah advisors' perception
   pertaining to the competitiveness of Islamic banks in Malaysia. This
   study employs a qualitative research approach and data was gathered
   through interviews. The findings of this study highlight the importance
   of three factors i.e., Islamic banks need to promote trustworthiness,
   competence and reliability. The study contributes to the body of
   knowledge pertaining to the development and competitiveness of Islamic
   banks in Malaysia, especially in facing strong competition from foreign
   banks.},
