   26-30, 1998},
Organization = {US DHHS, Agcy Tox Subst Dis Registry; NCI, Occupat Epidemiol Brach;
   NIEHS, Superfund Bas Res Program; Pan Amer Hlth Org; Univ Amer Puebla;
   World Meteorol Org},
Abstract = {At the city of Mexicali, the current method applied to the management of
   domiciliary solid waste has been burying the garbage without any
   previous treatment. This manner causes some others problems; because it
   is a big amount of garbage that always remains to open sky, and the
   strong winds that we frequently have in this city, transport all kind of
   materials, since remainders until microbes and fetid odors. The
   generation of solid waste has been one of the main problems that our
   authorities have to confront and a big part of the problem is focusing
   in the enormous amounts that everyday are picking up, management and
   sending to the final disposal place. With this, we can perceive the
   necessity of look for alternatives to have a good management of solid
   waste. In this study, we propose to take up the problem since its
   origins, this is, since the perception of the people living in one
   community at Mexicali about the management of solid waste. Also, we
   would like to establish with an environmental education program, an
   environmental culture about the suitable management of solid waste.},
