Note = {Annual International Conference on Social and Behavioural Sciences
   (ICSBS), Singapore, SINGAPORE, AUG 14-16, 2017},
Abstract = {This article aims to discuss Tun Mahathir's leadership communication
   from the Indian cultural perspective. Hence, the lived experience of the
   Indians in Malaysia on the leadership communication of Tun Mahathir was
   explored. Data were collected through a series of in-depth interviews
   with 15 informants including Malaysian-based Indian political leaders
   and ordinary citizens of the community. Three main themes were
   identified to explain the analysis outcomes: Tun Mahathir's leadership
   communication characteristics, the Indian cultural values that influence
   the perspectives of Indians towards Tun Mahathir's leadership
   communication, and Indian community's responses towards Mahathir's
   policies. This finding contributes to a new dimension of leadership
   communication study from cultural perspective specifically the Indian
   culture which is a minority group in Malaysia. Furthermore, it was found
   that the Indian culture particularly the religious values influences
   Indians' perception towards Tun Mahathir's leadership communication.
   Secondly, it was found that a leader with good understanding of
   followers' culture is able to bring development to the community. In
   addition, this paper also provides an insight to understand the
   leadership communication within the Indian community in Malaysia.},
