Note = {International Conference on Social Sciences and Humanities (SOSHUM),
   Kota Kinabalu, MALAYSIA, APR 19-21, 2016},
Abstract = {In order to penetrate the demands of customer requirements, the
   implementation of Quality Function Deployment (QFD) theory has been
   identified as a distinguished strategy, which is responsible in
   transforming customer requirements into product development or services.
   QFD has been adapted in most of the major manufacturer in Japan and
   United States and has been proven to reduce material waste and times
   production while improving the quality of product design. This shows
   that, the use of QFD can help SMEs entrepreneurs to improve their
   productivity and services in order to accommodate international markets.
   However, SMEs are facing challenges to implement and integrate QFD due
   to some factors. Therefore, the objective of this paper is to provide a
   review of the readiness among the SMEs in Malaysia apparel industry in
   implementing QFD. The method to review the perception and feedback from
   the SMEs are via survey and phone interviews among the apparel SMEs that
   are registered with SME Corp Malaysia. Analysis from the feedback was
   used to get the first impression of the level of readiness and current
   knowledge of the SMEs in order to stimulate QFD implementation in
   apparel Malaysia Industry in the future.},
