Year = {2013},
Pages = {45-48},
Note = {5th European Conference on Public Health, St Julians, MALTA, NOV 08-10,
   2012},
Abstract = {Purpose: The understanding about the importance of Quality of Life (QOL)
   has been increasing, following the change in the concept of Health.
   There is no doubt that there is more recognition and an awareness of the
   importance of acute coronary syndrome in individuals' QOL. We intend to
   relate the treatment of ACUTE MYOCARDIAL INFARCTION with QOL, bearing in
   mind that is a multidimensional, subjective and dynamic myocardial
   infarction concept. Methodology: It a quantitative and cross-sectional
   study was conducted. The sample consisted of 131 subjects with a medical
   diagnosis of acute myocardial infarction for at least six months. We
   used a validated questionnaire (sociodemographic characterization,
   clinical presentation and QOL - NewMac QLMI) self-applied by patients in
   an outpatient setting who attended at the outpatient hospital in Viseu.
   Results: We found that patients who underwent primary angioplasty had a
   better perception of QOL (F= 8.144, p=0.000; R-2=0.21). Conclusion: The
   assessment of perceived of QOL allows a better knowledge and adaptation
   to the patient's condition. We found that the type of treatment is a
   determining factor in QOL of individual's victims of acute coronary
   syndrome.},
