Note = {4th International Conference on Energy and Environment - Bringing
   together Engineering and Economics (ICEE), Guimaraes, PORTUGAL, MAY
   16-17, 2019},
Organization = {Univ Minho, Sch Engn; Univ Porto, Sch Econ \& Management; UP, Ctr Econ
   \& Finance; CentroAlgoritmi},
Abstract = {An adjusted characterization of the markets is a useful base for any
   marketing strategy, namely in sectors with great particularities as the
   wine markets, and for the sustainable plans. In fact, the perceptions
   and reactions of the consumers to strategies implemented in the wine
   sector are often different to those verified in others markets. For
   example, a high price for a wine bottle may be considered by the
   consumers as an attractive indicator of consumption for French wine and
   a bad indicator for wines from other specific regions. On the other
   hand, a lower price can be understood as a signal of weak wine quality.
   In this way, for the price definition in the wine markets, in a
   sustainable perspective, it is determinant to know the reaction of the
   consumers in each submarket. Considering this framework, the objective
   of this study is to analyse the export price elasticities of demand in
   each destination country. The elasticities price of demand
   quantification is important to assess the reaction of the consumers to
   the Portuguese wine prices. Of stressing that, the results show that the
   reaction of the consumers to the export prices changes is different for
   the diverse destination country.},
