   Acad Sci IR Iran; Latvian Acad Sci; Polish Acad Sci; Russian Acad Sci;
   Serbian Acad Sci \& Arts; Slovak Acad Sci; Natl Acad Sci Ukraine;
   Bulgarian Ind Assoc},
Abstract = {In this paper we present the relevance of orienting towards customer of
   the consumer services enterprises, making reference at the banking
   institutions, considering the extent to which they show some customer
   orientation and of the importance that it is providing to the services
   quality. Based on an example from the baking field we researched the
   importance of the factor orientation towards customer, of the report
   customer - bank and their influence on the banking institution. The
   research methodology is focused on research in the form of quasi -
   experiment. There were extracted two random samples with a total of 708
   customers (SMEs) from Galati, of whom 36.4\% being potentially loyal
   customers and 63.6\% potentially migratory clients. The report between
   the so called ``loyal customers{''} and ``migratory customers{''} was of
   48\% - 52\%. Following the questionnaires sent the feedback came from
   276 SMEs (38.98\%). The number of the questionnaires that could be
   exploited was of 252 because 24 questionnaires were incomplete. The
   conclusion in terms of content is that the perception of orienting
   towards customer is decisively influencing both the migration behavior
   as and the difference in the degree of customer's satisfaction.},
