Note = {International Conference on Education (ICOED), Jakarta, INDONESIA, APR
   12-14, 2016},
Abstract = {Cloud computing has viewed as one of the most discussed issues that
   promise to modernize traditional computing by providing visualized
   resources as a service over the internet. To stable in cloud computing
   acquisition requires an organization to address many of the same
   concerns they face in implementing an Information Technology (IT)
   service. This study encompasses the factors that affect the decision of
   cloud computing implementation in the management of various industries
   focuses on Software as a service (SaaS) platform. By synthesizing the
   literature from different sectors, this paper proposed a conceptual
   framework of a key driver of cloud computing implementation for Higher
   Education Institutions (HEIs). This conceptual framework extracted from
   the analysis of the Technology, Organization and Environment (TOE)
   framework and integrate with Diffusion of Innovation (DOI) theory. The
   four dimensions, particularly technology, organization, external
   environment and environmental sustainability, would be highlighted which
   could be used as a guideline to accelerate the implementation process of
   the computing technology in Malaysia education industry. Thus, the paper
   offered, would contribute cloud computing organization users and service
   provider with a better understanding and guidelines of cloud computing
   implementation characteristics with relevant perception on current
   services.},
