Note = {International Symposium on Sustainable-Development-of-City-Group,
   Changsha, PEOPLES R CHINA, NOV 16, 2009},
Organization = {Sustainable Dev City Grp; Cent S Univ, Hunan Inst Syst Engn \&
   Management},
Abstract = {Gray correlation analysis is adopted in the study of the relationship
   between industrial structure and industrial wastewater discharge in
   Pearl River Delta to examine their inherent associations. A quantitative
   analysis of recent 5 years' data was performed. The results showed that
   the correlation degrees between industrial wastewater discharge and
   gross output value of 10 industrial sectors for selected years all are
   bigger than 0.6, which meant that they all have a significant impact on
   industrial wastewater discharge, in which chemical engineering,
   papermaking industry and manufacture of medicines are the largest three
   sectors to affect the industrial wastewater emissions, while the effect
   of electronic equipment manufacturing industry is relatively small. It
   is concluded that traditional industry as the leading industry structure
   in Pearl River Delta will restrict the economical sustainable
   development and causes the constitutive pollution, electronic
   information industry should be given priority to the development in
   Pearl River Delta.},
