Note = {International Symposium on Sustainable-Development-of-City-Group,
   Changsha, PEOPLES R CHINA, NOV 16, 2009},
Organization = {Sustainable Dev City Grp; Cent S Univ, Hunan Inst Syst Engn \&
   Management},
Abstract = {This paper presents a laboratory study on the effect of redispersion
   emulsoid powder and cellulose ether on the performance of thermal
   insulating mortar with glazed hollow bead. The test results show that
   with the dosage of redispersion emulsoid powder increases, the
   consistency of thermal insulating mortar increases, apparent density,
   thermal conductivity and drying shrinkage decline, However, the
   compressive strength greater losses owing to excessive consumption of
   redispersion emulsoid powder; Cellulose ether within a certain dosage
   can significantly improve the operating performance of thermal
   insulation mortar, increase its consistency and reduce its apparent
   density, thermal conductivity coefficient and drying shrinkage. Due to
   excessive consumption of cellulose ether, the apparent density, thermal
   conductivity, compressive strength and drying shrinkage of thermal
   insulation mortar all increase. The operating performance of thermal
   insulation mortar become bad because of excessive consumption of
   redispersion emulsoid powder and cellulose ether. For a specific
   insulation mortar, there will exist the best mixing amount of
   redispersion emulsoid powder and cellulose ether.},
