   Changsha, PEOPLES R CHINA, NOV 16, 2009},
Organization = {Sustainable Dev City Grp; Cent S Univ, Hunan Inst Syst Engn \&
   Management},
Abstract = {Compared with traditional wastewater treatment process, biotrickling
   filter runs without aeration and sludge discharge. According to the
   principle of energy saving and low cost, three open biotrickling
   filters, filled with volcanics, bio-ceramic, and ceramic Pall ring have
   been designed to treat municipal sewage in the experiment. It is capable
   of ventilating naturally and no backwashing. The results suggest that
   volcanics and bio-ceramic present superiority on the removal of COD and
   NH(3)-N, especially both removal efficiency of COD and NH(3)-N through
   volcanics can reach as high as 83\% and 85\% and the effluent complies
   to GB18918-2002 1A. discharge standard. While removal efficiency of TN
   and TP are all far from expectation, which are needed further advancing.},
