Note = {International Symposium on Sustainable-Development-of-City-Group,
   Changsha, PEOPLES R CHINA, NOV 16, 2009},
Organization = {Sustainable Dev City Grp; Cent S Univ, Hunan Inst Syst Engn \&
   Management},
Abstract = {Due to the uncertainty and ambiguity about the slope's composition of
   geological conditions,the mechanical properties of rock
   mass,environmental factors etc it is very difficult to predict the
   degree of slope stability accurately. Because the study object of gray
   system theory is the uncertainty systerm of ``small sample{''}, ``poor
   information{''} which is ``partial known information,partial unknown
   information{''},so in this paper,by selecting some main factors which
   can affect the slope stability,and with the aid of the gray relational
   analysis of gray system theory,the author attempts to predict whether
   the slope will loose the stability, as well as order the weighings of
   main factors. The analysis of some slope engineerings shows that when
   analysing the slope,the usage of gray theory will reduce the impact of
   anthropic, subjective factors and enhance the reliability of slope
   analysis and evaluation.},
