Note = {2nd International Conference on Advanced Science and Information
   Technology (ASCIT), Cheonan, SOUTH KOREA, MAY 12-13, 2017},
Abstract = {Tambak Lorok has been selected as one of the maritim tourist
   destinations and a pilot project miniature of coastal area development.
   However, the condition is not idyllic without educational
   infrastructures and the residents ability to develop the tourist
   destination. The improvement of the educational infrastructures is
   actually needed by the residents to prepare the development into a
   tourist village. Library as a means of education can provide knowledge
   for the residents. Qualitative approach with narrative strategy used in
   this study to describe the attitude of fishermen on library. Fishermen
   are free to express their feelings, opinions, and tendencies on library.
   The data sources were the results of interviews with informants and a
   literature review. The result shows the attitude of fishermen on library
   in the forms of perceptions, feelings and tendencies. Library is
   perceived as a place to seek knowledge and a positive playground for
   children. The residents can read books and learn how to make fish,
   shrimp and squid into packaged food products, and change unused shells
   into ornaments for sale. The informants show a sense of excitement on
   library, which is proven by the expectation to have a village library
   which provides school books, creativity manuals, and books about
   recycling and flood prevention.},
