   JAPAN, MAR 21-25, 1998},
Organization = {Minist Educ Sci Culture \& Sports Japan; Okazaki Natl Res Inst; Natl
   Inst Physiol Sci; Pharmaceut Manufacturers Assoc Tokyo; Osaka Pharmaceut
   Manufacturers Assoc},
Abstract = {Sixty-six patients with chronic cerebral infarction (47 men and 19
   women, mean 64.0 +/- 11.9 years) underwent P300 event-related potentials
   (ERPs) and manifold neuropsychological testings, and we analysed the
   correlation between parameters of P300 ERPs and multimodality
   neuropsychological testings. Auditory and visual P300 ERPs were elicited
   by standard oddball paradigm. As to brain higher cortical functions,
   digit span, story recall test, verbal fluency test, trail making lest,
   letter cancellation test, RCPM, MMSE, and verbal paired associated
   learning test were examined.
   We used multiple regression analysis in order to clarify the correlation
   between P300 ERPs and brain higher cortical functions. Good models for
   P300 latency were obtained against manifold neuropsychological test
   results by high F value and coefficient of determination. Age
   contributed remarkably to the model in both auditory and visual
   paradigms. The RCPM test contributed to the model in auditory paradigm
   within the regression model. ERPs elicited by auditory paradigm seem to
   be related to the general intelligence based on visuospatial perception
   or analytical capacity. Meanwhile, visually evoked P300 might reflect
   complex visual scanning and tracking using a motor component or divided
   selective attention, since only TMT contributed to the model among the
   variables in the visual oddball paradigm.},
