Abstract = {In future, the German industry will be increasingly challenged by
   demographic issues and the so-called fourth industrial revolution
   (Industry 4.0) regarding workforce and organization of work. To approach
   these needs, a concept of demography management focusing on a holistic
   lifecycle management has been developed and field-tested in the
   production industry. This concept consists of three elements: (1)
   evaluation of the current demographic situation, (2) definition of
   strategic goals and (3) derivation of suitable measures for action. This
   paper focuses on the first element, the evaluation of the current
   demographic situation, which forms the basis of successful demography
   management. The results of the semi-standardized interviews, which have
   been developed and conducted within this element, are presented here.
   Through choosing the interviewees out of the principle of maximum
   contrast (e.g. assembly worker, production-related workers, managers),
   different perspectives have been taken into consideration to gather
   information about personal perceptions of demographic challenges and the
   current demography management. The analysis of the interviews aims at
   summarizing statements referring to the handling of demographic
   challenges as well as further adoptable measures. They have been
   clustered into categories by using Mayring's content analysis. The
   results are used as a preparation for the final derivation of action to
   implement and adjust a holistic demography management.},
